      "id": 1,
      "text": "Marriott-Slaterville was originally settled in 1852 by several Latter Day Saint pioneer families, including the Richard Slater family.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marriott-Slaterville%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Marriott-Slaterville officially became a city in July 1999 through a merger of the smaller communities of Marriott and Slaterville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://archivesspace.weber.edu/repositories/3/resources/506"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Descendants of J. Willard Marriott, the founder of Marriott International, still reside within the city of Marriott-Slaterville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marriott-Slaterville%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Marriott-Slaterville is located in Weber County and is part of the Ogden-Clearfield metropolitan area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marriott-Slaterville%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The city historian of Marriott-Slaterville prepares a monthly and yearly history book to document the local area.",
